1
00:00:06,139 --> 00:00:08,508
Whiskers and the Mosaic Bowl.

2
00:00:18,153 --> 00:00:22,279
Whiskers loved his big blue breakfast bowl more than anything.

3
00:00:22,479 --> 00:00:25,481
Good morning, bowl. You look delicious today.

4
00:00:29,931 --> 00:00:31,695
Whiskers, look! A butterfly!

5
00:00:37,562 --> 00:00:40,243
Oh no. My bowl. My beautiful bowl.

6
00:00:47,999 --> 00:00:50,336
Hola, gatitos! Why such sad faces?

7
00:00:50,536 --> 00:00:52,396
Whiskers broke his favourite bowl.

8
00:00:52,596 --> 00:00:56,262
Broken? Ay! In Barcelona, we never throw broken pieces away.

9
00:00:56,462 --> 00:00:58,590
Come with me, and I will show you a secret.

10
00:00:58,790 --> 00:01:00,711
Does the secret have food in it?

11
00:01:05,634 --> 00:01:10,552
So they sailed away on a big white ship, across the sparkling blue sea.

12
00:01:18,308 --> 00:01:20,943
Dolphins! Whiskers, look, real dolphins!

13
00:01:21,143 --> 00:01:25,081
I'm not looking. I'm keeping my breakfast where it belongs.

14
00:01:33,781 --> 00:01:35,715
Mira! There it is. Barcelona!

15
00:01:39,693 --> 00:01:43,971
La Rambla was full of flowers, music, and street performers.

16
00:01:51,255 --> 00:01:54,338
Luna. That golden statue just winked at me.

17
00:02:04,927 --> 00:02:08,524
Ole! Welcome, little friends! I am Paco, and this is my guitar.

18
00:02:08,724 --> 00:02:11,630
And you look hungry, amigo. Vamos, to the tapas!

19
00:02:11,830 --> 00:02:14,441
Finally, somebody who understands me.

20
00:02:18,891 --> 00:02:22,997
Tapas are little plates, so you can taste a bit of everything.

21
00:02:23,197 --> 00:02:26,251
Little plates? Then I will need a lot of them.

22
00:02:33,535 --> 00:02:37,187
Careful, amigo! The patatas bravas are a little bit spicy.

23
00:02:43,527 --> 00:02:46,578
A little spicy? My whiskers are on fire!

24
00:02:46,778 --> 00:02:49,406
Quick! Churros with hot chocolate. That will fix it.

25
00:02:56,218 --> 00:02:58,319
Whiskers, you have a chocolate moustache.

26
00:02:58,519 --> 00:03:01,677
I did that on purpose. It's very fashionable.

27
00:03:11,322 --> 00:03:16,933
Next, they visited the Sagrada Familia, with towers like giant sandcastles.

28
00:03:17,133 --> 00:03:18,815
Why are there cranes everywhere?

29
00:03:19,015 --> 00:03:22,689
They have been building it for over a hundred years. It is still not finished.

30
00:03:22,889 --> 00:03:25,954
Not finished? But it's already so beautiful.

31
00:03:26,154 --> 00:03:28,356
Exacto. Beautiful things take time.

32
00:03:37,529 --> 00:03:42,104
At the beach, full and happy, Whiskers fell asleep on the warm sand.

33
00:03:55,055 --> 00:03:56,690
Whiskers! Wake up! Your bowl!

34
00:04:02,085 --> 00:04:05,353
It's gone. All I have left is one little piece.

35
00:04:09,804 --> 00:04:12,865
Don't give up, Whiskers. Look what the sea brought us instead.

36
00:04:19,204 --> 00:04:22,352
Sea glass, polished by the waves! And a pretty shell, from me.

37
00:04:22,552 --> 00:04:25,838
Then Paco led them up the hill, to Park Guell.

38
00:04:32,178 --> 00:04:35,600
Whiskers, look! A giant lizard, made of colourful tiles!

39
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:39,388
Every tile was once broken. Gaudi turned the pieces into art.

40
00:04:39,588 --> 00:04:41,974
Broken pieces? Like my bowl?

41
00:04:42,174 --> 00:04:44,308
Just like your bowl. That is my secret.

42
00:04:55,842 --> 00:05:00,001
It's even better than before. It has a piece of everybody in it.

43
00:05:00,201 --> 00:05:02,124
Then tonight, we celebrate! Ole!

44
00:05:17,436 --> 00:05:22,361
Back home, Whiskers ate breakfast from the most beautiful bowl in the world.

45
00:05:22,561 --> 00:05:24,217
Wow! Where did you get that?

46
00:05:24,417 --> 00:05:28,821
Every piece is from a friend, Pip. The blue one is my old bowl.

47
00:05:29,021 --> 00:05:30,643
Can I add a piece too?

48
00:05:30,843 --> 00:05:32,899
There's always room for one more.

49
00:05:39,239 --> 00:05:44,410
Because broken things can shine again, when friends help put the pieces together.

